   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, but the app said it was delivered around 7 and I was sitting at home waiting. It wasn't there until 7:45, so it wasn't on time. $5.60 in credit doesn't really cover a 45 minute wait on dinner. Can you look at it again?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I did look at it again, Leo, and I agree with you. The courier's log confirms the order wasn't handed over until 7:47 PM. The \"delivered\" mark at 6:58 PM was wrong, because the courier was still 2.1 miles away. I based your compensation on the real handoff time, so it already counts the full 47 minutes you waited.\n\nPolicy sets the late-delivery compensation at 20% of the order subtotal, which is $5.60 for your order. It has to be account credit, and I can't add goodwill amounts beyond that. So I can't increase it.\n\nIf you'd like a person to review your case, I can pass it to a human specialist. They would follow up within 24 hours. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, so the app marked it delivered at 6:58 while the courier was still 2.1 miles away? That's the bit that annoys me most. Fine, yes, pass it to a human specialist. But I'm not happy with $5.60 as the answer, so I'd like them to look at whether it's fair."
  },
